Windows: two rustkit-layout tests added upstream (macOS develop 35034d6f, the chrome-board
work) pin macOS font behaviour and fail here (907 passed, 2 failed; found by refresh #16):

  test_an_emoji_label_lifts_a_styled_buttons_line
      expects an emoji label to lengthen a button's `normal` line by the emoji's FALLBACK face
      (Arial 14px: 16 -> 23, button 32 -> 39). measure_text_advanced does not unite the fallback
      face into the line on Windows, so the button stays 32. The existing test further down
      (n40) already skips when the platform does not unite fallback faces; this one gets the
      same guard. This is a gap in Windows text measurement, not merely a different number
      (the test's own comment says Blink unites the fallback face for any text line; I have NOT
      measured Chrome on Windows), so it is a skip, not a Windows expectation.
  test_negative_half_leading_inline_keeps_the_line_baseline
      pins Chrome-on-macOS metrics of the macOS system font: the stack
      `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif` resolves to Arial on Windows (the apply
      script's edit: Chrome on Windows does not know the macOS names), whose 32px bold seat is
      27 not 28 and whose 12px content area is 14 not 15. No Chrome-on-Windows numbers are
      pinned for this scenario, so rewriting the expectations from our own output would be
      circular: it is ignored on Windows with the reason.

Remove when upstream guards or parameterises both (hiwave-macos row filed from refresh #16).

